# Edge vhost for freecad.virtastic.app — deployed as a drop-in into the shared edge Caddy's
# sites dir (on the VPS: /opt/edge/sites/freecad.caddy; imported by /opt/edge/Caddyfile via
# `import sites/*.caddy`). The shared edge terminates TLS with the Cloudflare Origin cert and
# reverse-proxies to the freecad container by name on the shared docker network.
#
# The container's own nginx already sets COOP/COEP/CORP (required for SharedArrayBuffer); those
# response headers pass through this reverse_proxy. So this vhost deliberately does NOT set them
# again (duplicate COOP/COEP breaks crossOriginIsolated) and does NOT `encode` (would interfere
# with the large raw .wasm/.data and Range requests).
freecad.virtastic.app {
	tls /certs/virtastic.crt /certs/virtastic.key
	# sec_headers sends X-Frame-Options SAMEORIGIN for every site on this edge. FreeCAD is
	# meant to be embedded (?embed=1, GitHub #3), so this vhost alone drops it. Embedding
	# still needs the host page to be cross-origin isolated, which no header here can grant.
	# BEFORE the import: the snippet's block is deferred (it deletes a header), deferred
	# header ops run innermost first, and after it this delete ran first and was overwritten
	# (measured: the deploy's edge check still saw SAMEORIGIN). The outermost runs last.
	header -X-Frame-Options
	import sec_headers
	reverse_proxy freecad:80
}
